All **15 tests pass** — 10 failures reduced to 0. Here's a summary of the 9 bugs fixed across 3 modules:

### `src/auth.py` (2 bugs → 3 test failures fixed)
- **`has_permission`** — case-sensitive comparison. Now lowercases both `required` and each role.
- **`is_admin_or_owner`** — used `and` instead of `or`. Admin **or** owner should grant access, not both.

### `src/inventory.py` (4 bugs → 4 test failures fixed)
- **Mutable default arg** — `initial={}` was shared across all instances, so `Inventory()` instances shared the same stock dict. Changed to `None` + fresh dict per instance.
- **`add` overwriting** — used `=` instead of accumulating. Now does `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`.
- **`reserve` boundary** — `qty >= available` rejected reservation of the full stock. Changed to `>` so reserving everything available is allowed.
- **`release` no guard** — allowed reserved count to go negative. Now raises `ValueError` when release qty exceeds reserved.

### `src/text_utils.py` (3 bugs → 3 test failures fixed)
- **`slugify` not lowercasing** — added `text.lower()` at the top.
- **`slugify` only collapsed one `--` pair** — `replace("--", "-")` is single-pass. Replaced with `re.sub(r"-+", "-")`.
- **`truncate` added suffix beyond max_len** — `text[:max_len] + suffix` produced an 11-char string for max_len=10. Changed to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`.
